{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-truth-phone-components-1-a-01","date":"2026-11-25","lens":"2","surface":"phone","area":"phone/components-1","refs":["F-phone-1316"],"severity":"S3","title":"The Strength score counts curls, flyes, triceps work and heavy machines as the big five lifts","what":"The Charts page says the Strength score uses bench press, squat, deadlift, overhead press and row. In fact any exercise whose name contains bench, squat, deadlift, overhead, shoulder press or row is used. So an Incline Bench Preacher Curl or a Flat Bench Cable Fly can stand in for the bench press, an Overhead Triceps Extension or an Overhead Cable Curl for the overhead press, and an Upright Row for the row. A member who does none of the real lifts gets a low score from these small moves. A member who uses the Hack Squat, Belt Squat or a row machine gets a high score from machine weights, which the score then compares with barbell standards.","expected":"Only the real five lifts (and close barbell versions) feed the score, as the info text promises, so the 0 to 100 number means the same for every member.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/services/analytics.ts:122","apps/mobile/src/services/analytics.ts:133","apps/mobile/src/engine/strength.ts:9-15","apps/mobile/src/engine/strength.ts:29-36","apps/mobile/src/components/analytics/StrengthSection.tsx:47-50","apps/mobile/src/tracker/catalog/catalogData.ts:159","apps/mobile/src/tracker/catalog/catalogData.ts:166","apps/mobile/src/tracker/catalog/catalogData.ts:182","apps/mobile/src/tracker/catalog/catalogData.ts:249"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"strength-lifts-matched-by-name-words","who":"members","how_often":"every time a member logs one of these look-alike exercises and not the real lift","fix_line":"Pick the five lifts by a fixed list of exercises instead of words in the name","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
